Wed Oct 28 08:53:47 UTC 2026 - John Paul Adrian Glaubitz <adrian.glaubitz@suse.com>

- Update to version 20261022.00
  * Update Go toolchain and module dependencies, this also updates
    golang.org/x/net to v0.61.0 (bsc#1287488, CVE-2026-97032)
  * Reduce Linux snapshot service gRPC keepalive interval and add
    post-snapshot failsafe watchdog
  * Implement support for `InstanceSetup.NetworkEnabled` flag in the core plugin.
  * Support extracting ISV versions from discovered process fields.
- from version 20261015.00
  * Ensure OS Login configuration on disk is rolled back on startup when
    OS Login is disabled in metadata, even if the boot disk or image
    previously had OS Login enabled.
  * Add `remove_state` field to `StopRequest` and deprecate `cleanup`.
  * Update Guest Telemetry Extension to version 1.2 bringing several
    security improvements.
  * Avoid storing plugin state if the plugin is a local plugin, and clean up
    existing state files for local plugins.
  * [MWLID] Don't return an error on `GetStatus` if `lastError` is not nil.
  * [MWLID] Initialize `galog`.
  * Fix TestCheckExpiredKey to use valid OpenSSH authorized key format
  * Force network configuration reload when another manager rolls back state.
  * Update go mod dependencies.
  * Update incorrect comments. Remove redundant check.
  * Support falling back to stderr for version command output.
  * Update protoc generated header comments to v7.36.0.
  * Update go mod dependencies.
  * Respect both the `disable-address-manager` metadata key and the `disable`
    configuration flag under the `AddressManager` section of the configuration file.
  * Exactly match the legacy implementation of the `sshd_config` for OS Login.
  * Only log "No local plugins to install" if there are actually no plugins.
  * Respect the `sysprep-specialize` configuration flag in the `MetadataScripts`
    section of the configuration file.
  * No public description
  * No public description
  * Fix order-dependent tests.
  * Update env vars to support separate intervals for scan and report
  * Update command arguments for disabled shells.
  * Ensure USE_DISCOVERED_PROCESS_PATH commands run as the discovered process user.
  * When cleaning up `NetworkManager` network configuration files, use `os.Remove`
    instead of `os.RemoveAll`
  * Update guest_telemetry_extension to version 1.1.
  * Avoid writing the private PEM key if MDS returns empty content for the endpoint.
  * Refresh credentials when the identity UUID is changed, and defer the next timed
    refresh.
  * Skip core plugin installation if it doesn't exist.
  * Ignore requests from ACS for uninstalling local plugins, and all requests for
    the core plugin.
  * Refactor workloadcertrefresh late-loaded module into an independent extension.
